        "subject": "LU-20947 o2iblnd: keep a PUT_DONE with a posted send attached",
        "message": "LU-20947 o2iblnd: keep a PUT_DONE with a posted send attached\n\nA scheduler can handle a PUT_ACK before the PUT_REQ send completes.\nIf connd finalises the conn in that window, kiblnd_queue_tx_locked()\nputs the PUT_DONE on ibc_zombie_txs and clears tx_conn. The send\ncompletion then calls kiblnd_tx_complete() with a NULL conn.\n\nA PUT_DONE with a posted send now goes back on ibc_active_txs with\nits conn ref. The send completion then releases it.\n\nFixes: a155c3fca38d (\"LU-11756 o2iblnd: kib_conn leak\")\nTest-Parameters: trivial nettype=o2ib testlist=sanity-lnet\nSigned-off-by: Chris Horn <chorn@ddn.com>\nAssisted-by: ClaudeCode:claude-opus-5-5\nChange-Id: I595ee2d1401d244d5134c69f622d5a574da541cc\n"
      },
      "branch": "refs/heads/master"
    }
  },
